From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:38:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] epic_panel: a read-only dock panel of the project's epic
 stories

A project planned with the epic plugin keeps its stories under .epic/,
and the only overview of them was .epic/EPIC.md: an index the plugin
regenerates only when it runs epic-index.sh, so it is usually stale.
This adds an "Epic Stories" dock panel that reads the story files
themselves and follows them while they change. Story 042, phase 1.

What it adds:

  * crate epic_panel, a dock panel on the 0035 pattern: action
    `epic panel: toggle focus`, the right dock by default, the position
    kept in the KVP store, registered in initialize_panels. Its dock
    button shows only while a local worktree has .epic/ at its root.
  * One row per directory of .epic/stories/ and, under a collapsed
    "Archived (N)" header, of .epic/archive/: number, slug, status and
    the tasks.md checkbox progress "<closed>/<total> (+<n> deferred)".
    Spikes show their verdict ("promote to <N>"), superseded stories
    "superseded by <N>", with " (missing)" when no directory carries
    that number; an unknown status is shown as written, with a warning.
    The tooltip carries the title and type/scale/engineering. Enter or a
    click opens story.md (else tasks.md) in a tab; "Open EPIC.md" opens
    the index. Several .epic worktrees get one header each; rows stop at
    2000 with "N more not shown". Keyboard: Up/Down, Enter.
  * Live updates: Fs::watch on .epic/ plus Watcher::add on every area
    and story directory it reads (.epic/ is usually gitignored, so the
    worktree scanner cannot be relied on for it), one rescan per 500 ms.
    A watch that fails shows "Live updates are off: <reason>. Use
    Refresh." and Refresh keeps working.

Why a patch: a Zed extension cannot render a panel or dock button.

The grammar is the plugin's, not YAML: format.rs ports epic plugin
0.13.1's epic-index.sh line for line (front_value, census,
parse_verdict, the status and progress cells; ASCII trim, as the
script runs under LC_ALL=C). The script is byte-identical in plugin
0.18.0. parity_tests.rs is the contract that guards it: with
EPIC_PARITY_DIR and EPIC_INDEX_SH set, it runs the real epic-index.sh on
a temp copy of a corpus and compares every row's number, status and
progress with the panel's; zero rows fails, every disagreement is
listed. On this workspace's .epic/: 57 rows, 0 mismatches.

It writes nothing and runs nothing. .epic/ is read only through
Arc<dyn Fs> (metadata, read_dir, load); a file over 1 MiB is left
unread ("too large"), a symlinked story directory or file is never
followed, and an unreadable file marks its row, never the scan.
never_writes_tests.rs scans a RealFs corpus (symlinks and a FIFO
included) and a panel-session test drives a whole session over one;
both find every name, byte, mtime and link target unchanged. A static
guard checks the crate's non-test sources name no mutating Fs method,
no std::fs and no process API. Logs are key=value lines
(event=scan ... duration_ms=, event=problem, event=watch_failed) and
never carry file content or an absolute path.

Phase 2 (not in this patch) lets a row send its slash command
(`/epic:epic stories run <id>`, the id being the row's directory name)
to an agent thread, prefilled and never sent, so the plugin stays the
only writer of .epic/. It goes through 0045's
AgentPanel::new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt, which needs a source
session the panel does not have, so phase 2 adds a `pub` sibling
without one, the way 0052 added open_new_thread_for_devtools. Phase 1
takes no agent_ui dependency.

Packaging: USE epic, its own series group after devtools-panel and
before test. Generated on top of the claude-agent-acp-plus group (its
zed wiring sits beside 0035's agent_tasks_panel), so REQUIRED_USE ties
the two. It applies with claude-code-ide and devtools-bridge each on or
off, and 0050/0051 apply on top of it unchanged. No new third-party
crate: Cargo.lock gains only the epic_panel entry.

One hunk sits outside the crate, in crates/fs: RealFs::metadata warns
when a symlink's target cannot be read, and that warning printed the
whole path. A hostile symlink inside an untrusted repository's .epic/
would put an absolute path in the log the panel promises never to
write one to, so the warning now names the file only. Behaviour is
otherwise unchanged; the panel_fs_log test pins it.

The plugin was renamed Epico (2026-11-03): it now keeps `.epico/` with
the index in `EPICO.md`, between `epico:index` markers, written by
`epico-index.sh`, and its migrate-dir.sh moves a project's `.epic/` to
`.epico/` the next time it runs there. The panel reads `.epico/` first
and falls back to `.epic/` (index `EPIC.md`) for a project not moved
yet; with both present the plugin moves nothing and writes `.epico/`, so
that is the one read. The labels follow ("Epico Stories", "Open
EPICO.md", "No .epico/ directory in this project"); the action and the
panel's persistence key keep `epic_panel`/`EpicPanel`, so saved keymaps
and dock positions survive. The grammar did not change: epico 0.25.1's
epico-index.sh is epic 0.21.0's epic-index.sh with the names replaced,
and the parity contract now runs against it.

Tests: epic_panel, 188 tests (grammar 5 files, scan, watch, the panel's rows,
shell, open, live updates and field contract, never-writes, parity,
the fs symlink log line).
